NorwayChartPreview=Chart import preview
NorwayChartScope=Preview changes nothing. Confirmed import creates only new accounts; existing accounts, mappings and entries are preserved. Account labels are compared exactly. Ledger usage counts each number in the active entity, including previous charts. Product, third-party and line mappings are not inspected. This does not confirm Norwegian chart suitability or SAF-T mapping.
NorwayChartFormat=Format norway-chart-csv/1: UTF-8, semicolon, header account_number;label. One account per line, 4–8 digits without a leading zero, label 1–255 bytes. Maximum 1000 accounts and 256 KiB. Select an active chart associated with Norway first.
NorwayChartCSV=Paste CSV
NorwayChartRun=Show preview
NorwayChartNumber=Account number
NorwayChartLabel=Proposed label
NorwayChartExisting=Existing label
NorwayChartUsage=Ledger lines
NorwayChartStatus=Result
NorwayChartStatusNew=New account – not created
NorwayChartStatusKeep=Keep existing account
NorwayChartStatusConflict=Conflict – existing account preserved
NorwayChartStatusInactive=Inactive account – preserved
NorwayChartStatusHistorical=Historical account number – investigate
NorwayChartInvalidChart=Select an active chart associated with Norway in accounting settings. Preview unavailable.
NorwayChartInvalidCSV=Invalid CSV, duplicate or exceeded limit. The entire preview was rejected.
NorwayChartReadError=Could not read chart or ledger. Preview unavailable.

NorwayChartConfirm=Confirm creation of new accounts
NorwayChartConfirmScope=Confirm only after review and with a recent backup. This preview can be confirmed for ten minutes. No default accounts, tax codes or SAF-T mapping are set. CSV is temporarily held in your server session until confirmation, replacement or expiry.
NorwayChartBlocked=Import blocked: resolve conflicting, inactive or historical account numbers first.
NorwayChartImported=Created %s new accounts. Existing accounts and entries were preserved.
NorwayChartChanged=Preview expired, changed or lacks valid confirmation. Create a new preview. No accounts were imported.
NorwayChartImportFailed=Import could not be confirmed. Create a new preview and check stored accounts before retrying.

NorwayProfile=Install Norwegian chart of accounts
NorwayProfileScope=Norwegian chart with 745 accounts from Odoo l10n_no (LGPL-3), pinned to a documented revision. Confirmed installation creates and selects the chart for an empty accounting setup. An empty stock selection can be replaced only when the entity has no accounts or ledger history. Existing accounts or history are not replaced. No default accounts, tax codes or SAF-T mapping are set. Review suitability for your business; this is not a complete or professionally approved accounting solution.
NorwayProfileConfirm=Install or complete Norwegian chart
NorwayProfileInstalled=Norwegian chart selected. Created %s new accounts. Check default accounts, journals and VAT setup separately.
NorwayProfileBlocked=The Norwegian chart cannot be installed now. Another chart, existing accounts/history, conflicts, changed preview or a technical failure requires review. No existing chart is replaced.

NorwayAccountingSuggestions=Account suggestions for the Norwegian chart
NorwayAccountingSuggested=Suggested account
NorwayAccountingSuggestionsScope=Suggestions are not saved. 1500 and 2400 cover customer receivables and supplier payables. 3020 covers domestic service sales at the high VAT rate for VAT-registered businesses; it is not a general rule for foreign sales or sales without VAT. 2700 and 2710 cover the high rate; deduction entitlement, tax codes and VAT registration require separate assessment. Choose purchase accounts according to the expense. Assign 1920 to the actual bank account in bank settings. Transfer and suspense accounts require separate choices. Existing defaults, entries and journals are preserved. Product, customer/supplier and line mappings may override default accounts.

NorwayBankSetup=Bank and cash mapping checks
NorwayBankSetupScope=Lists open bank and cash accounts for the active entity. The ledger account must exist and be active in the selected chart. The journal must be active, have a code and be of bank/cash type. NOK is checked against the module sales scope. Sharing a ledger account across open accounts is flagged for review. Available confirms only that the mapping exists; it does not certify account classification, bank reconciliation or balances. Closed accounts and historical movements are not examined. No settings or payments are changed.
NorwayBankSetupEmpty=No open bank or cash accounts found. Create an account and select its ledger account and bank journal before posting payments.
NorwayBankSetupAccount=Bank/cash account
NorwayBankSetupLedger=Ledger account
NorwayBankSetupJournal=Linked journal
NorwayBankSetupCurrency=Currency
NorwayBankSetupShared=Shared ledger account
NorwayBankSetupSharedAvailable=Not shared
NorwayBankSetupSharedReview=Used by multiple accounts – review
NorwayBankSetupCash=Cash
NorwayBankSetupOpen=Open bank and cash accounts

NorwayWizard=Norwegian setup wizard
NorwayWizardScope=This wizard groups Norwegian setup for one entity and NOK sales documents. It reads settings without saving choices or providing production approval. Passing a check does not certify Norwegian accounting compliance.
NorwayWizardOverview=Show all eleven steps
NorwayWizardCurrent=Checks in the current installation
NorwayWizardCurrentVAT=Current VAT setting — not evidence of historical registration
NorwayWizardSettings=Open relevant settings and checks
NorwayWizardPrevious=Previous step
NorwayWizardNext=Next step
NorwayWizardGuide=Read the full Norwegian setup guide and official sources
NorwayWizardNoSave=Navigation does not save progress. Next step only opens the next page. Document manual decisions separately and distinguish unresolved, not applicable and missing functionality.
NorwayWizardUsers=Users and permissions
NorwayWizardPartners=Customers and suppliers
NorwayWizardProducts=Products and services
NorwayWizardInvoiceSettings=Invoice settings
NorwayWizardProposalSettings=Proposal settings
NorwayWizardPeriods=Fiscal years and periods
NorwayWizardTitle1=Business and scope
NorwayWizardBody1=Establish entity form, startup or migration, fiscal year, delivery model, countries and customer types. Record staff, physical cash sales, payment providers and special conditions. Distinguish software licences, downloads and SaaS/subscriptions where treatment differs.
NorwayWizardLimit1=Manual assessment. The initial development profile is a sole proprietor without staff selling software. Other entity forms and special rules are not automatically qualified.
NorwayWizardTitle2=Company, currency and access
NorwayWizardBody2=Enter the registered name, organisation number, full address and Norway as country. Use NOK as base currency. Create individual users with appropriate permissions. Check HTTPS and administrator access.
NorwayWizardLimit2=The checks below cover required fields, number format and base currency. They do not verify registry identity, permissions or historical company information.
NorwayWizardTitle3=VAT status and treatment
NorwayWizardBody3=Confirm actual registration and effective date from the decision before invoicing VAT. Starting to invoice does not automatically register the business. Assess domestic sales and purchases, exemptions, the pre-registration period and reverse charge. Assess deduction entitlement separately.
NorwayWizardLimit3=The current VAT setting and registry lookup are not a registration timeline. Norwegian tax codes, historical periods and a complete VAT report remain unfinished. Missing 15/12 percent rates do not imply software sales should use those rates.
NorwayWizardTitle4=Chart, accounts and journals
NorwayWizardBody4=Install the Norwegian chart with preview and confirmation if setup is empty. Review defaults for customers, suppliers, sales, purchases and VAT. Check active coded journals of the correct types: sales, purchases, bank/cash and general. Product, partner and line mappings may override defaults.
NorwayWizardLimit4=745 accounts do not mean 745 decisions to make. The setup check offers suggestions without saving them automatically. An existing account does not certify classification or tax treatment. Account categories and SAF-T/reporting mappings remain unfinished.
NorwayWizardTitle5=Banking and payments
NorwayWizardBody5=Create or edit the actual bank account. Select NOK, a ledger account and an active bank journal. Check payment information on the invoice. Assess payment references, providers, fees and partial payments separately. Cheques must not be used.
NorwayWizardLimit5=Checks cover open bank/cash accounts and structural mappings. They do not certify balances, classification or reconciliation. Closed accounts and historical movements are not examined. Bank integration and complete reconciliation remain unfinished.
NorwayWizardTitle6=Customers, suppliers and software
NorwayWizardBody6=Record correct names, addresses, countries and organisation/tax identity where applicable. Select Norwegian or English per customer. Configure the appropriate product/service type, delivery description, NOK price, tax treatment and sales account. Document subscription delivery periods.
NorwayWizardLimit6=Manual review. This page does not inspect all product or partner mappings. Free text is not translated automatically and invoice timing alone does not determine period allocation.
NorwayWizardTitle7=Proposals, invoices and credit notes
NorwayWizardBody7=Choose automatic numbering, payment terms, bank information and document models before the first invoice. Check Norwegian and English documents for seller/customer identity, delivery details, amounts, VAT and due date. Credit notes must reference the original invoice. Assess any entity-specific registry wording.
NorwayWizardLimit7=Basic checks and tested PDF models are available, but not every Norwegian requirement for every model. NOK and the language setting below do not verify numbering or document contents. Do not delete issued documents to correct errors.
NorwayWizardTitle8=Public customers and foreign trade
NorwayWizardBody8=For public customers, establish the EHF recipient, buyer/order reference, contract and access point. For foreign trade, establish delivery model, recipient country and customer type for each sales/purchase scenario. EUR display is only indicative; sales documents demand NOK.
NorwayWizardLimit8=PDF is not EHF. Qualified Norwegian EHF/Peppol and foreign tax treatment remain unfinished. Do not use zero percent as a blanket foreign-trade rule. Bank conversion does not automatically resolve accounting for foreign purchases.
NorwayWizardTitle9=Opening balances, periods and routines
NorwayWizardBody9=On migration, reconcile bank, open receivables/payables, VAT, assets, liabilities and equity against the previous system at the same date. Preserve source documents. Set the fiscal year and document allocation, approval, locking and correction routines. Separate private/business movements and assess owner transactions by entity form.
NorwayWizardLimit9=Chart import does not migrate balances or open items. Complete migration reconciliation, Norwegian specifications and qualified period locking remain unfinished. The voucher check does not replace bank, subledger or VAT reconciliation.
NorwayWizardTitle10=Reporting, retention and operations
NorwayWizardBody10=Assign responsibility for VAT returns, tax/business returns and any annual accounts filing. Document retention, storage country, privacy and access. Arrange recurring backups, a separately secured copy and a restore drill. Assess employer and cash-register duties where applicable.
NorwayWizardLimit10=Norwegian SAF-T export and direct filing are not available. Low turnover alone does not exempt electronic accounting from SAF-T. Updates take backups, but a copy on the same server is not a complete retention strategy. See official sources in the guide.
NorwayWizardTitle11=Review before use
NorwayWizardBody11=Document decisions, reasons, owner, date and evidence for each step. Distinguish unresolved from not applicable. Test each applicable chain using synthetic data in a separate environment: document, posting, payment/credit note, reconciliation and reporting/export. Review supported scope and gaps with the accounting lead.
NorwayWizardLimit11=This is the final guidance page, not a completion button. No overall green status is calculated. Unfinished VAT, EHF, SAF-T and history support are delivery gaps that cannot be approved by clicking next.
NorwayWizardDocumentLanguages=Language selection on sales documents

NorwayDefaults=Save customer and supplier accounts
NorwayDefaultsScope=Fills only empty customer (1500) and supplier (2400) defaults in an unused accounting setup with the shipped Norwegian chart. Existing and inherited choices, including different account numbers, are preserved. Validated customer/supplier invoices or ledger history block filling. Sales, purchase and VAT accounts, journals, banks and entries are not changed.
NorwayDefaultsEffective=Effective installation value
NorwayDefaultsFill=Fill empty choice after confirmation
NorwayDefaultsKeep=Preserve existing choice
NorwayDefaultsBlocked=Filling blocked. Check the selected Norwegian chart, active accounts with unchanged names, and invoice/ledger history. Review manually when the setup is already in use.
NorwayDefaultsConfirmScope=Review the proposals and have a recent backup before confirmation. Confirmation applies to this preview for ten minutes. Settings are checked again when saving.
NorwayDefaultsConfirm=Confirm filling empty choices
NorwayDefaultsSaved=Saved %s account defaults. Existing choices were preserved.
NorwayDefaultsFailed=Saving could not be confirmed. Create a new preview and check stored values before retrying.
NorwayDefaultsNothing=No empty choices to fill. Existing choices are preserved; this does not verify that all mappings are correct.

NorwayJournals=Create missing journal types
NorwayJournalsScope=Proposes only missing active sales, purchase, bank and general journal types. Existing active coded journals are preserved regardless of name or code. Inactive journals are not activated. Proposed codes are project defaults, not authority codes. Bank accounts, mappings and entries are not changed.
NorwayJournalsCreate=New journal after confirmation
NorwayJournalsKeep=Preserve existing journals
NorwayJournalsBlocked=Creation blocked: a proposed code already exists without covering the journal type. Review existing journals manually. No journals are replaced or activated.
NorwayJournalsConfirmScope=Review proposals and have a recent backup before confirming. Confirmation applies to this preview for ten minutes. The journal register is checked again when saving. Bank accounts must still be linked to their appropriate bank journal.
NorwayJournalsConfirm=Confirm creation of missing journals
NorwayJournalsSaved=Created %s journals. Existing journals and entries were preserved.
NorwayJournalsFailed=Creation could not be confirmed. Create a new preview and check the journal register before retrying.
NorwayJournalsNothing=All four journal types have active coded journals. This does not verify bank mappings or correct posting.

NorwayCompanyFieldsHelp=Open Company/organisation and save Norway as the country first. Under company identifiers: the organisation number is nine digits without NO or MVA. Legal form is the registered form, such as ENK or AS; select it yourself. The VAT number is a separate field for registered businesses and does not replace the organisation number. Do not add VAT registration wording before registration is confirmed. The VAT-liable setting and registration effective date require separate assessment. Updating does not select a legal form or change numbers or VAT status.
